<title>USA: Cardiac Pathways gets heart device okay.</title>
<headline>Cardiac Pathways gets heart device okay.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cardiac Pathways Corp said Wednesday that the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has granted approval of the company's 510(k) application to commercially release its Arrhythmia Mapping System for use in the diagnosis of patients with abnormally rapid heart rhythms, or tachyarrthymias.</p>
<p>The company said it plans to begin shipping the Arrhythmia Mapping System in the U.S. market in August 1997.</p>
</text>
